    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0244" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.003 Wallace, Henry A./63a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-25T22:00:00-04:00">May 25, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>720. Department recently sent you texts of statements by President and Vice
                        President<anchor n="33" xml:id="d214-f1"/> concerning latter’s visit to
                    China. Following are arrival dates principal points on journey: Washington to
                    Edmonton May 20, Fairbanks 21st (Cross date line lose one day), Anadyr 23rd,
                    Yakutsk 31st, Irkutsk June 5, Semipalatinsk 15th, Tashkent 17th, Alma Ata 20th,
                    Tihwa 22nd, Chungking 23rd, Kunming 26th, Kweilin 28th, Chengtu 30th, Sian,
                    Tungkuan and Lanchow July 2, Ulan Bator 3rd, Chita 5th. Arrive in United States
                    9th.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
